aprsc has carried the core of the APRS-IS network for well over a decade. Its
module decomposition — separating packet parsing, q-construct handling,
duplicate detection, server-side filtering, the client registry, and the
incoming/outgoing packet paths into distinct, individually testable units — is
a genuinely good design, and aprsr's crate and module layout deliberately
follows it. `docs/architecture.md` records the correspondence module by module.
Our thanks to the authors for publishing that design openly.

IMPORTANT — aprsr contains NO source code, configuration files, documentation,
or web assets from aprsc. aprsr is an independent implementation written from
the public APRS-IS protocol specifications published at http://www.aprs-is.net/
(notably the Connecting, q construct, and javAPRSFilter documents). aprsc was
consulted as an architectural reference only. Because aprsr is distributed
under MIT OR Apache-2.0 rather than aprsc's BSD-3-Clause, this separation is
maintained deliberately and is a standing rule for all contributions; see
AGENTS.md.


